ocus the refinement on a\n  specific observation. Set `global_=True` to target the global harness store\n  (cross-session); omit for local (session-scoped) refinement.\n\n## Rules\n\n- Refinement never runs mid-cell. A scheduled refinement runs when the current\n  turn ends; the harness applies changes and rebuilds the system prompt, then\n  resumes you automatically. Continue working normally after calling it.\n- One request per turn is enough; calling `run` again before the turn ends only\n  updates the instructions.\n- Use refinement after observing a repeated failure, a reusable tactic, a\n  repeated delegation role, or a behavior policy worth persisting. Do not\n  rewrite the whole harness when a focused memory, skill, prompt note, or\n  subagent spec is enough.\n\n"},{"type":"tool","name":"ipython","input":"await refine.run('Create a global memory for task-76e8f616 with caution: demos show same-size grids and transform certain repeated pattern regions by coloring continuation cells 1, but exact rule unresolved. Demo1: rows with long contiguous 5 bar on background9 had trailing cells recolored 1 (e.g. width11 row with 9 initial 5s, trailing 2 become 1; full-width bar unchanged). Demo2 similar width20 bars of 18 fives get last two cells 1; full-width bar unchanged. Demo3/4 show repeated motif continuation in blank background colored 1, including vertical alternating patterns. Task test used background8, foreground5, 12x27 with pattern clusters at rows1-2 and9-10; no solution validated. Important error: submissions were often reported “not a valid ARC grid”; ensure every output row length exactly consistent with expected width and output cell integers 0-9 before submission. The task behavior is unresolved, do not present a guessed rule as confirmed.', global_=True)","t":1790695064.123913,"output":"{'scheduled': True, 'note': 'Refinement runs when the current turn ends; applied edits are appended to your context as a refinement notice and you resume automatically.